<http://data.silknow.org/object/f06bda01-32ef-3bd0-8cb9-e661e288247d/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Description: Lacis; silk net darned with silk.\nTwo groups, each of three diagonal red silk threads, knotted in white silk to form a diamond shaped lattice. The lower part forms a border with three lines of darning.  At either end of the border there are two S-motifs.  Otherwise the two motifs are a diamond shaped arrangement of nine tiny flower heads and a flower with two leaves forming alternate bands.\nOne end has been cut irregularly."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f06bda01-32ef-3bd0-8cb9-e661e288247d> .

